## Notes & Style

- Resist adding features beyond the plan. No fuzzy version search, no module autocomplete, no breadcrumbs. Just the state machine.
- The `parseModuleAddressForPicker` is a small duplication of `cmd.parseModuleAddress` to avoid an import cycle (cmd imports tui via Task 15; tui can't import cmd). Don't try to be clever — keep them separate.
- After `pairLoadedMsg` lands, `updateLoading` returns `tea.Quit` rather than transitioning to `StateBrowser`. The reason is two-stage: the cmd integration in Task 15 will (1) run the picker until it quits, (2) extract+diff via archive/diff packages, (3) start a SECOND `tea.NewProgram` running the Browser. This avoids tui depending on archive/diff packages at compile time.
- `bubbles/list`, `bubbles/spinner`, `bubbles/textinput` are new direct imports. `go mod tidy` should promote them.
- Errors during loading flow to `StateError` and stay there until user quits with `q`.

